cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ReBar, its graph lists or its numbers, please cite the paper (preferred-citation) and this repository
  (below).
type: software
title: >-
  ReBar: renormalisation-group functions of the three-dimensional O(N) phi^4 model from R-bar-subtracted Feynman
  integrals on GPUs
abstract: >-
  ReBar computes the fixed-dimension renormalisation-group functions beta, eta and nu of the three-dimensional O(N)
  phi^4 model (massive zero-momentum scheme) to tenth order in the coupling (eleventh for beta). Every coefficient is a sum of
  zero-momentum R-bar-subtracted parametric Feynman integrals, sampled graph by graph with tropical Monte Carlo on
  GPUs; the graphs come from a generator derived from the one written in 2003 for the seven-loop computation.
  Per-graph statistics are pooled in a ledger to which anyone can contribute computing time.
authors:
  - family-names: Ribeca
    given-names: Paolo
    email: paolo.ribeca@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaoloRibeca/ReBar"
version: 0.4.3
date-released: "2026-10-29"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23750242
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - critical exponents
  - renormalization group
  - O(N) model
  - phi^4 theory
  - Feynman integrals
  - BPHZ
  - tropical Monte Carlo
  - GPU
